{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794554244,"nonce":"HS9vmEAOSd8x8ncQp2UfP9anydc=","title":"Landed scroll, hover and FLIP work has only run in the harness","message":"The work from the GPU-deferral scroll and animation commits is held by the headless harness (rows against a full paint, frame by frame). Nothing below has been looked at in a window, and it needs a person at the machine: the pointer cannot be driven for you.\n\n- Scrolling: `cargo run --release -p blinc_app_examples --example scroll_bench` with LIST=virtual and LIST=flat, pointer over the list while it scrolls. Watch for pauses, and for colours and text out of step (37795b1e).\n- Hover follows content (89a690c8): a still pointer over a list that scrolls under it. The synthetic move runs once per frame in which a scroll offset or the layout changed and hover reacts to something, and it is not throttled. Check the cost with many hover rules.\n- A wide hover rule (`.list:hover .row`) over a long list with the pointer moving: frame cost.\n- A cn tabs reorder slide (cn_demo), FLIP on rows (241a0233): no label left at the old position, and no flash on the frame the slide ends, which is painted in full because the binding is released.\n- The slide is evaluated on the CPU each frame; evaluating it from the frame clock is P2b in 122c606.\n\niOS and Android are in their own issue.","files":null}]}